  "rule": "An Arabic noun has three grammatical cases: Raf' (nominative – the doer / subject), Nasb (accusative – the one the action falls on), and Jarr (genitive – after a preposition or as the second term of an idafa). I'rab is shown either by vowel marks (damma, fatha, kasra) or by letters (-āni, -ayni, -ūna, -īna).",
  "note": "I'rab by vowel marks applies to the singular noun, while in the dual and sound plural, letters do the work of I'rab.",
